<!-- CHAPTER 1: INTRODUCTION -->
<h1 class="chapter">1. Introduction</h1>

<h2 class="section">1.1 Overview</h2>
<p>The hospitality industry is one of the largest and fastest-growing sectors of the global economy. Hotels, resorts, and guest houses serve millions of travellers every day and face the critical challenge of efficiently managing room inventory, customer bookings, payments, and guest communication. In many small and medium-sized hotels, especially in developing countries, room booking and management are still done using manual methods such as paper-based registers, phone-based reservations, and disconnected spreadsheets. These traditional approaches have numerous disadvantages including the risk of duplicate bookings, inaccurate room availability records, delayed guest communication, data loss, and difficulty in generating financial and occupancy reports.</p>
<p>With the advent of the internet and web technologies, customers increasingly expect the ability to search for rooms, compare prices, check availability in real time, and make bookings and payments online without visiting the hotel in person or calling the front desk. Hotels that fail to provide an online presence with booking capabilities risk losing customers to competitors who do. Furthermore, the increasing use of chatbots and AI-powered assistants in customer service has raised guest expectations for instant, 24/7 responses to common questions about room availability, pricing, check-in/check-out times, and hotel policies.</p>
<p>The <strong>Hotel Room Booking Website with Assistant Chatbot</strong> is a full-stack web application built with Python and the Django 6.0 framework following the MVT (Model-View-Template) architecture. It provides a unified platform for both hotel administrators and customers. Administrators can manage room types, rooms, staff, bookings, payments, and customer enquiries through a secure backend interface. Customers can browse rooms, search with advanced filters, book rooms, make payments via Razorpay, interact with an AI-powered chatbot, and reset passwords via email OTP. The system also generates PDF booking receipts and sends automated email confirmations.</p>

<h2 class="section">1.2 Problem Statement</h2>
<p>Many small and medium-sized hotels in developing countries still manage room bookings using manual methods such as paper registers, phone-based reservations, and disconnected spreadsheets. These traditional approaches suffer from several critical disadvantages:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Double Booking Risk:</strong> Without real-time availability checking, two or more guests may be booked for the same room on overlapping dates, leading to embarrassing situations and guest dissatisfaction.</li>
<li><strong>Inaccurate Records:</strong> Guest information, room details, and booking records may be duplicated across multiple registers or spreadsheets, leading to inconsistencies.</li>
<li><strong>Slow Retrieval:</strong> Searching for a specific booking, guest record, or payment history in a paper register or large spreadsheet is time-consuming and error-prone.</li>
<li><strong>No Online Presence:</strong> Many small hotels do not have a website or online booking system. Customers must visit in person or call, limiting the hotel's customer reach.</li>
<li><strong>No Automated Communication:</strong> Booking confirmations, reminders, and other communications are sent manually. There is no system for sending confirmation emails, OTPs, or notifications.</li>
<li><strong>No 24/7 Assistance:</strong> Without a chatbot or automated FAQ system, guest enquiries can only be answered during front-desk working hours.</li>
<li><strong>Delayed Payment Processing:</strong> Payments are typically collected at check-in or check-out in cash. There is no facility for advance online payment.</li>
<li><strong>Difficult Reporting:</strong> Generating summary reports for occupancy rates, revenue, or demographics is extremely labour-intensive.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="section">1.3 Solution to the Problem</h2>
<p>The proposed solution is a web-based Hotel Room Booking System with the following key features:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Centralized Database:</strong> A PostgreSQL relational database storing all hotel data in normalized tables with referential integrity, eliminating data redundancy and inconsistency.</li>
<li><strong>Online Booking with Overlap Detection:</strong> Customers can browse, search, and book rooms online. The system automatically detects date-range overlaps to prevent double booking.</li>
<li><strong>Secure Online Payments:</strong> Integration with Razorpay payment gateway enables customers to pay using credit/debit cards, UPI, and net banking.</li>
<li><strong>AI Assistant Chatbot:</strong> A rule-based chatbot provides instant responses to common queries about rooms, staff, bookings, and hotel policies.</li>
<li><strong>AJAX-Powered Search:</strong> Advanced room search with real-time filtering by name, type, price range, and date availability without page reload.</li>
<li><strong>Automated Email Notifications:</strong> Booking confirmations and OTP-based password reset via Django SMTP email.</li>
<li><strong>Admin Management:</strong> Secure backend for CRUD operations on room types, rooms, staff, and for viewing bookings, payments, and customer enquiries.</li>
<li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Bootstrap 5.3 ensures the website works seamlessly on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.</li>
<li><strong>PDF Generation:</strong> Downloadable booking receipts in PDF format using the xhtml2pdf library.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="section">1.4 Existing System</h2>
<p>Before developing the proposed system, a thorough study of the existing hotel management practices was conducted. In many small and medium-sized hotels, the following manual and semi-automated systems are in use:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Paper-Based Booking Register:</strong> Room bookings are recorded manually in a physical register or diary. The receptionist writes the guest name, contact details, room number, check-in date, check-out date, and amount in the register. This register is the primary source of booking information.</li>
<li><strong>Phone-Based Reservations:</strong> Customers call the hotel to enquire about room availability and make reservations. The receptionist checks the register manually, informs the caller about availability, and records the booking on paper or in a simple spreadsheet.</li>
<li><strong>Spreadsheet-Based Records:</strong> Some hotels use Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets to maintain booking records, guest information, and payment details. While this is an improvement over paper registers, it still requires manual data entry and does not provide real-time availability checking.</li>
<li><strong>No Online Presence:</strong> Many small hotels do not have a website or online booking capability. Customers must visit the hotel in person or call to check availability and make bookings, which is inconvenient and limits the hotel's reach.</li>
<li><strong>No Automated Communication:</strong> Booking confirmations, reminders, and other communications are sent manually via phone calls or occasionally by email. There is no automated system for sending confirmation emails, OTPs, or notifications.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="section">1.5 Objectives</h2>
<ol>
<li>To design and develop a web-based hotel room booking system that automates room type management, room inventory management, booking management, staff management, and customer contact management using the Django web framework and Python programming language.</li>
<li>To provide customers with a user-friendly, responsive web interface for browsing hotel room categories, viewing room details (with images, prices, and descriptions), and searching for rooms using advanced filters including room name, room type, price range, and check-in/check-out date availability.</li>
<li>To implement date-range-based availability checking logic that prevents double booking of the same room by detecting overlapping check-in and check-out dates before confirming any booking.</li>
<li>To integrate an online payment gateway (Razorpay) for secure transaction processing so that customers can pay for their bookings online using credit cards, debit cards, UPI, and net banking.</li>
<li>To build an intelligent assistant chatbot that can classify user queries into categories (room, staff, booking, general) and provide relevant, context-aware responses.</li>
<li>To implement advanced room search functionality with real-time AJAX-based filtering that returns results without full page reload.</li>
<li>To incorporate email notification services for booking confirmations and OTP-based password recovery.</li>
<li>To generate downloadable PDF reports of booking details using the xhtml2pdf library.</li>
<li>To maintain secure access control through user authentication, session management, CSRF protection, and input validation.</li>
<li>To follow Software Engineering practices and the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) throughout the development process.</li>
</ol>
<div class="pb"></div>

