<!-- CHAPTER 3: REQUIREMENT SPECIFICATION -->
<h1 class="chapter">3. Requirement Specification</h1>

<h2 class="section">3.1 Overall Description</h2>

<h3 class="subsec">3.1.1 Product Perspective</h3>
<p>The Hotel Room Booking System is a new, self-contained web application developed from scratch. It replaces manual hotel booking processes with an automated online system. The product operates as a client-server web application accessible through standard web browsers. It communicates with a PostgreSQL database server for data persistence and integrates with external services including Razorpay (payments) and Gmail SMTP (email). The system follows the Django MVT architecture where Models define the data structure, Views handle the business logic, and Templates render the user interface.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">3.1.2 Product Functions</h3>
<p>The system provides two main interfaces with distinct functions:</p>
<p><strong>Customer-Facing Website:</strong> Home page with room type categories, about page, services page, rooms listing, advanced room search (AJAX), booking form with date overlap detection, booking cart with tax calculation, Razorpay payment integration, user registration and login, password reset via email OTP, contact form, chatbot widget, team page, and PDF receipt generation.</p>
<p><strong>Administrator Backend:</strong> Secure admin login, dashboard with navigation, room type CRUD, room CRUD with foreign key to room types, staff CRUD, booking records viewer, payment totals viewer, customer contact messages viewer, and Django Admin interface for chatbot and notification management.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">3.1.3 User Characteristics and Classes</h3>
<p><strong>Customers:</strong> End-users who browse rooms, search for availability, make bookings, process payments, interact with the chatbot, and reset passwords. They require a simple, intuitive interface with clear navigation and minimal training. Customers may access the system from desktop, tablet, or mobile devices.</p>
<p><strong>Administrators:</strong> Hotel staff who manage room inventory, staff profiles, view booking and payment records, and respond to customer enquiries. They require a secure backend interface with efficient data management tools.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">3.1.4 Constraints</h3>
<ul>
<li>The system requires Python 3.10 or higher and Django 6.0 installed on the server.</li>
<li>PostgreSQL database server must be running and accessible.</li>
<li>Internet connectivity is required for Razorpay payment integration and email notifications via SMTP.</li>
<li>The system is designed for single-hotel use only. Multi-branch management is a future enhancement.</li>
<li>Responsive design requires modern web browsers (Chrome 120+, Firefox 120+, or Edge 120+).</li>
<li>Minimum hardware: dual-core processor, 4 GB RAM, 20 GB free disk space.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="section">3.2 Specific Requirements</h2>

<h3 class="subsec">3.2.1 Functional Requirements</h3>
<p><strong>Administrator Functional Requirements:</strong></p>
<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A01</td><td>Admin Login</td><td>Admin shall log in using Django's built-in authentication (username and password).</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A02</td><td>Admin Logout</td><td>Admin shall securely log out, destroying the session.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A03</td><td>Add Room Type</td><td>Admin shall add room types with name, description, and image.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A04</td><td>View/Edit/Delete Room Types</td><td>Admin shall view, modify, and delete room types.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A05</td><td>Add Room</td><td>Admin shall add rooms linked to a room type, with name, price, description, and image.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A06</td><td>View/Edit/Delete Rooms</td><td>Admin shall view, modify, and delete rooms.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A07</td><td>Add Staff</td><td>Admin shall add staff with name, designation, social links, and photo.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A08</td><td>View/Edit/Delete Staff</td><td>Admin shall view, modify, and delete staff records.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A09</td><td>View Bookings</td><td>Admin shall view all booking records with customer, room, dates, and price.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A10</td><td>View Payments</td><td>Admin shall view payment records with customer, mobile, and total amount.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A11</td><td>View Contact Messages</td><td>Admin shall view and delete customer contact messages.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-A12</td><td>Manage Chatbot</td><td>Admin shall manage chatbot responses, conversations, and notifications via Django Admin.</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Customer Functional Requirements:</strong></p>
<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C01</td><td>User Registration</td><td>Customer shall register with username, email, and password.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C02</td><td>User Sign-In</td><td>Customer shall sign in with username and password, creating a session.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C03</td><td>Browse Rooms</td><td>Customer shall browse room categories and view rooms of a specific type.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C04</td><td>Advanced Search</td><td>Customer shall search rooms by name, type, price range, and dates via AJAX.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C05</td><td>Book a Room</td><td>Customer shall book a room with date/guest details and overlap detection.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C06</td><td>View Booking Cart</td><td>Customer shall view booked rooms with subtotal, tax, and total.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C07</td><td>Make Payment</td><td>Customer shall pay via Razorpay using card, UPI, or net banking.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C08</td><td>Chatbot Interaction</td><td>Customer shall send messages to the chatbot and receive contextual responses.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C09</td><td>Password Reset</td><td>Customer shall reset password via email OTP verification.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C10</td><td>Contact Enquiry</td><td>Customer shall submit a contact form with name, email, phone, subject, and message.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-C11</td><td>Email Confirmation</td><td>Customer shall receive booking confirmation email after successful booking.</td></tr>
</table>

<h3 class="subsec">3.2.2 Non-Functional Requirements</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Category</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>Security</td><td>CSRF protection on all forms. ORM-based parameterised queries prevent SQL injection. Template auto-escaping prevents XSS. Session-based authentication with server-side session storage.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Usability</td><td>Responsive design supporting desktop (1920px), tablet (768px), and mobile (375px). Consistent navigation and layout. Intuitive form design with validation feedback.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reliability</td><td>Input validation on all forms. Graceful error handling with user-friendly messages. Date-overlap detection prevents booking conflicts.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Maintainability</td><td>Modular Django app structure (Backend and webapp apps). Separation of concerns. URL routing follows Django conventions.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Performance</td><td>Pages load within 2-3 seconds on broadband. AJAX search results appear in under 1 second. Database queries optimized with Django ORM.</td></tr>
</table>

<h3 class="subsec">3.2.3 Performance Requirements</h3>
<p>Web pages shall load within 2-3 seconds on a broadband connection. AJAX search results and chatbot responses shall appear within 1 second of the request. The database shall support at least 50 concurrent users without significant performance degradation. The system shall handle peak-hour loads without crashing.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">3.2.4 External Interface Requirements</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Payment Gateway:</strong> Razorpay REST API for order creation (amount, currency), payment capture, and transaction verification. Test mode (sandbox) used during development.</li>
<li><strong>Email Service:</strong> Django SMTP email backend configured for Gmail. Used for sending booking confirmation emails and password reset OTPs.</li>
<li><strong>Web Browser:</strong> Application must render correctly and function fully in Chrome 120+, Firefox 120+, and Edge 120+.</li>
<li><strong>Database:</strong> PostgreSQL 16 with support for SQL standards, foreign keys, and concurrent read/write operations.</li>
<li><strong>File Storage:</strong> Local file system storage for uploaded images (room type images, room images, staff photos).</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="subsec">3.2.5 System Evolution</h3>
<p>The modular Django architecture allows easy addition of new features as separate apps without affecting existing code. The database schema can be extended through new migration files. API endpoints can be versioned for backward compatibility.</p>

<h2 class="section">3.3 Use Case Diagram</h2>
<p>The system has two primary actors: <strong>Customer</strong> and <strong>Administrator</strong>.</p>

