<!-- CHAPTER 4: DESIGN DOCUMENT -->
<h1 class="chapter">4. Design Document</h1>

<h2 class="section">4.1 Modularization Details</h2>

<h3 class="subsec">4.1.1 Front-End Modules</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Home Page Module:</strong> Displays room type category cards with images and descriptions. Each card links to the filtered rooms page. Includes navigation bar, footer, and floating chatbot widget.</li>
<li><strong>About / Services / Team Modules:</strong> Hotel information page, services listing with icons, and team display with staff profile cards showing photos, names, designations, and social media links.</li>
<li><strong>Room Browsing Module:</strong> Room categories overview, filtered rooms by type, and all rooms listing with images, prices, descriptions, and Book Now buttons.</li>
<li><strong>Advanced Search Module:</strong> AJAX-powered filter panel with inputs for room name, room type dropdown, minimum price, maximum price, check-in date, and check-out date. Results update dynamically without page reload.</li>
<li><strong>Booking Module:</strong> Booking form with date pickers, guest count inputs, special request textarea, and automatic price calculation. Date-overlap detection prevents double booking.</li>
<li><strong>Cart Module:</strong> Displays booked rooms with subtotal, tax (10% or 20% based on subtotal), and total. Includes delete buttons and proceed-to-payment option.</li>
<li><strong>Payment Module:</strong> Razorpay integration with order creation and payment popup supporting cards, UPI, net banking, and wallets.</li>
<li><strong>Authentication Module:</strong> Sign-up form, sign-in form, and password reset flow (email verification, OTP entry, new password form).</li>
<li><strong>Contact Module:</strong> Contact form with name, email, phone, subject, and message fields with validation.</li>
<li><strong>Chatbot Module:</strong> Floating chat widget with message input, send button, chat history display, suggestion chips, and room card rendering for room queries.</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="subsec">4.1.2 Back-End Modules</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Room Type Management:</strong> Add room type (name, image, description), display all types in a table, edit type details, delete type (cascade deletes associated rooms).</li>
<li><strong>Room Management:</strong> Add room (type dropdown FK, name, image, price, description), display all rooms, edit, delete.</li>
<li><strong>Staff Management:</strong> Add staff (name, designation, Facebook, Instagram, image), display all staff, edit, delete.</li>
<li><strong>Booking Management:</strong> View all booking records with customer name, email, room, dates, guests, and total price.</li>
<li><strong>Payment Management:</strong> View all payment totals with customer name, mobile, and amount linked to bookings.</li>
<li><strong>Contact Management:</strong> View and delete customer contact messages.</li>
<li><strong>Chatbot API Module:</strong> POST endpoint for processing user messages, classifying queries (room/staff/booking/general), and generating responses.</li>
<li><strong>Advanced Search API Module:</strong> GET endpoint returning filtered room data as JSON with availability checking.</li>
<li><strong>Notification API Module:</strong> GET/POST endpoints for retrieving and marking notifications as read.</li>
<li><strong>Django Admin Module:</strong> Built-in admin interface for managing chatbot responses, conversations, and notifications.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="section">4.2 Data Integrity</h2>

<h3 class="subsec">4.2.1 Product Data (Room Data)</h3>
<p>Room and room type data is stored in two tables. The roomtypedb table stores room categories (Luxury, Deluxe, Standard, Budget) with names, descriptions, and images. The roomnamedb table stores individual rooms with a foreign key to roomtypedb (one-to-many: one type has many rooms). Room prices are stored as integers in Indian Rupees (INR). Image files are validated through Django's ImageField. When a room type is deleted, all its associated rooms are deleted via CASCADE.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">4.2.2 User Data</h3>
<p>Customer registration data is stored in the Registerdb table with fields for username, password (stored as plain text for simplicity, to be enhanced with hashing), confirm password, and email (validated via Django's EmailField). User sessions are managed through Django's session framework with server-side storage. Admin users are managed through Django's built-in User model with PBKDF2 password hashing.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">4.2.3 Order Data (Booking Data)</h3>
<p>Booking records are stored in the bookingdb table with foreign keys to Registerdb (CUSTOMER, SET_NULL on delete) and roomnamedb (SELECTROOM, CASCADE on delete). Each booking captures check-in/check-out dates, guest counts, special requests, and total price. Payment records are stored in Totaldb with a foreign key to bookingdb (CASCADE). The overlap detection logic uses: existing booking's check-in <= new check-out AND existing booking's check-out >= new check-in.</p>

<h2 class="section">4.3 Procedural Design</h2>

<h3 class="subsec">4.3.1 User Registration and Login</h3>
<p><strong>Registration:</strong> The user fills in username, email, password, and confirm password. The view creates a new Registerdb object and saves it. A success message redirects to the sign-in page.</p>
<p><strong>Login:</strong> The user enters credentials. The view queries Registerdb for a matching record. If found, the username is stored in the session and the user is redirected home. If not, an error is displayed.</p>
<p><strong>Password Reset:</strong> The user enters their email. A 5-digit OTP is generated, stored in session, and sent via email. The user enters the OTP; if it matches (after whitespace stripping), a new password form appears. If passwords match, the password is updated and a confirmation email is sent.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">4.3.2 Room Browsing and Selection</h3>
<p>The home page displays room type category cards. Clicking a category shows filtered rooms. Each room displays its image, name, type, price, and a Book Now button. The advanced search page allows filtering by name, type, price range, and dates via AJAX.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">4.3.3 Cart (Booking Cart)</h3>
<p>After booking, the customer is redirected to the cart page showing all bookings with room name, dates, and price. The system calculates subtotal (sum of room prices), tax percentage (10% if subtotal > Rs 5000, else 20%), and final total. Each row has a delete button.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">4.3.4 Payment Processing</h3>
<p>The customer enters their mobile number and proceeds to payment. The amount is multiplied by 100 (Razorpay works in paise). A Razorpay client creates an order with the amount and currency (INR). The Razorpay checkout popup opens for payment via card, UPI, or net banking.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">4.3.5 Order Confirmation</h3>
<p>After successful booking, an automated email confirmation is sent to the customer via Django SMTP. The booking details are visible in the admin panel. Customers can download a PDF receipt via the generate_pdf view using xhtml2pdf.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">4.3.6 Administrative Functions</h3>
<p>Administrators log in through a secure admin login using Django's authenticate() and login() functions. The admin dashboard provides access to all management functions: room type CRUD, room CRUD, staff CRUD, booking viewer, payment viewer, contact viewer, and Django Admin for chatbot management.</p>

<h2 class="section">4.4 User Interface Design</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Consistent Navigation:</strong> Fixed-top navbar with hotel logo, menu items (Home, About, Services, Rooms, Contact), and authentication links on all customer-facing pages.</li>
<li><strong>Card-Based Layout:</strong> Room types, rooms, and staff profiles displayed as Bootstrap cards with images and descriptions.</li>
<li><strong>Responsive Grid:</strong> Bootstrap 5.3 grid system adapting from desktop (3-column) to tablet (2-column) to mobile (single-column).</li>
<li><strong>Color Scheme:</strong> Professional blues, neutral greys, and accent colors for CTAs.</li>
<li><strong>Admin Backend:</strong> Star Admin2 theme with sidebar navigation and tabular data displays.</li>
<li><strong>Chatbot UI:</strong> Floating bottom-right button opens gradient purple chat window with message bubbles and suggestion chips.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="section">4.5 Database Design</h2>
<p>The database consists of 10 tables normalized up to 3NF. The roomtypedb table stores room categories with id, ROOMTYPE, ROOMTYPEIMAGE, DESCRIPTION. The roomnamedb table stores individual rooms with id, ROOMTYPE FK, ROOMNAME, ROOMIMAGE, ROOMPRICE, ROOMDESCRIPTION. The Registerdb table stores customer accounts. The bookingdb table stores bookings with foreign keys to Registerdb and roomnamedb. The Totaldb table stores payments linked to bookings. The staffdb table stores staff profiles. The customercontactdb table stores enquiries. Three chatbot tables (ChatbotResponse, ChatbotConversation, Notification) support the chatbot system. All tables use auto-generated integer primary keys and enforce referential integrity through foreign key constraints.</p>
<div class="pb"></div>

