<h2 class="section">6.2 Integration Testing</h2>

<h3 class="subsec">6.2.1 User Authentication Integration Test</h3>
<p>Tested the complete flow from registration to login to booking. A user registers, logs in (session created), and books a room. The booking's CUSTOMER foreign key correctly links to the Registerdb record. Result: Pass.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">6.2.2 Room Search Integration Test</h3>
<p>Tested the flow from room type creation to room addition to search results. An admin creates a room type, adds a room under it, and the advanced search API correctly returns the room with its type name. Result: Pass.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">6.2.3 Booking and Ordering Integration Test</h3>
<p>Tested the end-to-end booking pipeline: room selection, booking form, overlap detection, cart calculation, payment record creation with FK, and email notification. All steps executed successfully. Result: Pass.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">6.2.4 Admin Panel and Database Integration Test</h3>
<p>Tested the complete admin cycle: login, add room type, add room, add staff, view bookings, view payments, view contacts, logout. All CRUD operations successful with correct data persistence. Result: Pass.</p>

<h2 class="section">6.3 Code Improvement</h2>

<h3 class="subsec">6.3.1 Refactoring</h3>
<p>The chatbot logic was separated into dedicated handler functions (handle_room_query, handle_staff_query, handle_booking_query, handle_general_query) instead of a single monolithic function. The booking overlap detection was extracted into a reusable query pattern. Template URLs were consolidated using Django's URL template tags.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">6.3.2 Optimization</h3>
<p>Database queries were optimized using Django's select_related() for foreign key lookups. Chatbot conversations and notifications were indexed on username and created_at fields for faster retrieval. AJAX search responses were minimized to include only essential room data.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">6.3.3 Code Reviews</h3>
<p>Regular code reviews identified potential issues, ensured consistent coding style, and verified edge case handling including empty inputs, missing images, invalid dates, and null foreign key references. Reviews focused on security (CSRF, SQL injection prevention) and error handling.</p>

<h3 class="subsec">6.3.4 Version Control</h3>
<p>Git was used for version control throughout the project lifecycle. All changes were committed with descriptive messages. The repository includes the complete development history and requirements.txt for dependency management.</p>
