<div class="pb"></div>

<!-- CHAPTER 9: LIMITATIONS -->
<h1 class="chapter">9. Limitations of the Project</h1>
<ol>
<li><strong>OS Requirement:</strong> Requires modern OS (Windows 10+, Linux, macOS) with Python 3.10+ support.</li>
<li><strong>Software Dependencies:</strong> Requires Python, Django, PostgreSQL, and supporting libraries installed.</li>
<li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Dual-core processor, 4-8 GB RAM recommended for multiple concurrent users.</li>
<li><strong>Rule-Based Chatbot:</strong> Uses keyword matching, not NLU. Complex queries may not be understood.</li>
<li><strong>Plain-Text Passwords:</strong> Customer passwords stored as plain text (PBKDF2/Argon2 hashing recommended).</li>
<li><strong>Single-Hotel:</strong> Designed for single hotel use; no multi-branch support.</li>
<li><strong>No Dynamic Pricing:</strong> Prices are fixed; no demand-based adjustment.</li>
<li><strong>No Refunds:</strong> Automated refunds not implemented; manual processing required.</li>
<li><strong>No Mobile App:</strong> Web-only; no native Android/iOS app available.</li>
</ol>
<div class="pb"></div>

<!-- CHAPTER 10: FUTURE APPLICATION -->
<h1 class="chapter">10. Future Application of the Project</h1>
<ol>
<li><strong>Dynamic Pricing:</strong> Auto-adjust prices based on demand, season, and occupancy.</li>
<li><strong>Loyalty Program:</strong> Rewards system and discount coupon codes.</li>
<li><strong>Multi-Hotel:</strong> Central dashboard for multiple branches.</li>
<li><strong>NLP Chatbot:</strong> ML-based understanding using OpenAI/Hugging Face.</li>
<li><strong>OTA Integration:</strong> Sync with Booking.com, MakeMyTrip, Goibibo.</li>
<li><strong>Advanced Payments:</strong> Refunds, GST invoices, EMI, wallet support.</li>
<li><strong>Review System:</strong> Customer ratings and reviews with aggregate scores.</li>
<li><strong>SMS Notifications:</strong> Twilio/MSG91 integration for booking alerts.</li>
<li><strong>Cloud Deployment:</strong> AWS, Google Cloud, or DigitalOcean hosting.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile App:</strong> React Native/Flutter for Android and iOS.</li>
<li><strong>Multi-Language:</strong> Django i18n for global customers.</li>
<li><strong>Room Amenity Tagging:</strong> Filter by Wi-Fi, AC, TV, Mini-bar.</li>
</ol>
<div class="pb"></div>

<!-- CHAPTER 11: CONCLUSION -->
<h1 class="chapter">11. Conclusion</h1>
<p>The <strong>Hotel Room Booking Website with Assistant Chatbot</strong> project was successfully designed, developed, and tested as part of the BCSP-064 course requirement. The system addresses the real-world need for an affordable, web-based hotel booking solution that automates room management, customer booking, payment processing, and guest communication.</p>
<p>All ten objectives were met: a full-stack Django application, responsive Bootstrap interface, date-overlap booking prevention, Razorpay payment integration, rule-based chatbot, AJAX search, email notifications, PDF reports, secure access control, and SDLC-aligned development with thorough testing.</p>
<p>The system was tested at unit (25 tests), integration (4 scenarios), system, and user acceptance levels with all tests passing. Eight bugs were identified and resolved during testing. The database follows 3NF with 10 interconnected tables. The modular architecture allows easy addition of new features.</p>
<p>The project demonstrates competence in Python programming, database management, web development, software engineering, and AI-assisted user interaction - core subjects of the BCA programme. The system is fully functional and ready for deployment in a real hotel environment.</p>
<div class="pb"></div>

